-0.006781420204788446,-0.21431255340576172,-0.001789517467841506,-0.0090705007314682,-0.6380290389060974,-0.0010804060148075223,-3.576278118089249e-07,-0.009100506082177162,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.000427274004323408,-2.3841855067985307e-07,0.0,0.0,-4.768370445162873e-07,-7.152555099310121e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-4.768360213347478e-06,-2.9802276912960224e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,79,2075,15087,387,264,40899,47311,1741,429,400,79,4080,18,8,284,481,21,4779,400,79,7,19,8,284,220,23,4779,400,79,7,20,8,284,220,16,15,4779,323,400,79,7,22,8,284,220,16,20,2418,220,7379,400,79,7,16,17,568,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $p(x)$ be a cubic polynomial such that $p(-3) = -6,$ $p(4) = 8,$ $p(5) = 10,$ and $p(7) = 15.$  Find $p(12).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"71139bdb14bb803fe2e2936d0be51c2573319c04479e4cf476e9e968c71abdbf"},"seconds":106.46419167518616,"seed":1146106098054575830,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\( p(12) \\) where \\( p(x) \\) is a cubic polynomial, we need to find the coefficients of the polynomial. A general cubic polynomial is given by:\n\\[\np(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\n\\]\nWe are given the following conditions:\n\\[\np(-3) = -6, \\quad p(4) = 8, \\quad p(5) = 10, \\quad p(7) = 15\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the polynomial, we get four equations:\n1. For \\( x = -3 \\):\n\\[\na(-3)^3 + b(-3)^2 + c(-3) + d = -6 \\implies -27a + 9b - 3c + d = -6\n\\]\n2. For \\( x = 4 \\):\n\\[\na(4)^3 + b(4)^2 + c(4) + d = 8 \\implies 64a + 16b + 4c + d = 8\n\\]\n3. For \\( x = 5 \\):\n\\[\na(5)^3 + b(5)^2 + c(5) + d = 10 \\implies 125a + 25b + 5c + d = 10\n\\]\n4. For \\( x = 7 \\):\n\\[\na(7)^3 + b(7)^2 + c(7) + d = 15 \\implies 343a + 49b + 7c + d = 15\n\\]\n\nWe now have the system of linear equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n-27a + 9b - 3c + d = -6 \\\\\n64a + 16b + 4c + d = 8 \\\\\n125a + 25b + 5c + d = 10 \\\\\n343a + 49b + 7c + d = 15\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nWe can solve this system step-by-step. First, we eliminate \\( d \\) by subtracting the first equation from the second, the second from the third, and the third from the fourth:\n\\[\n(64a + 16b + 4c + d) - (-27a + 9b - 3c + d) = 8 - (-6) \\implies 91a + 7b + 7c = 14 \\implies 13a + b + c = 2\n\\]\n\\[\n(125a + 25b + 5c + d) - (64a + 16b + 4c + d) = 10 - 8 \\implies 61a + 9b + c = 2\n\\]\n\\[\n(343a + 49b + 7c + d) - (125a + 25b + 5c + d) = 15 - 10 \\implies 218a + 24b + 2c = 5 \\implies 109a + 12b + c = \\frac{5}{2}\n\\]\n\nNow we solve the reduced system:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n13a + b + c = 2 \\\\\n61a + 9b + c = 2 \\\\\n109a + 12b + c = \\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nSubtract the first from the second:\n\\[\n(61a + 9b + c) - (13a + b + c) = 2 - 2 \\implies 48a + 8b = 0 \\implies 6a + b = 0 \\implies b = -6a\n\\]\n\nSubtract the second from the third:\n\\[\n(109a + 12b + c) - (61a + 9b + c) = \\frac{5}{2} - 2 \\implies 48a + 3b = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies 16a + b = \\frac{1}{6}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( b = -6a \\) into \\( 16a + b = \\frac{1}{6} \\):\n\\[\n16a - 6a = \\frac{1}{6} \\implies 10a = \\frac{1}{6} \\implies a = \\frac{1}{60}\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -6a = -6 \\left( \\frac{1}{60} \\right) = -\\frac{1}{10}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) into \\( 13a + b + c = 2 \\):\n\\[\n13 \\left( \\frac{1}{60} \\right) - \\frac{1}{10} + c = 2 \\implies \\frac{13}{60} - \\frac{6}{60} + c = 2 \\implies \\frac{7}{60} + c = 2 \\implies c = 2 - \\frac{7}{60} = \\frac{113}{60}\n\\]\n\nFinally, substitute \\( a, b, c \\) into one of the original equations to find \\( d \\):\n\\[\n64a + 16b + 4c + d = 8 \\implies 64 \\left( \\frac{1}{60} \\right) + 16 \\left( -\\frac{1}{10} \\right) + 4 \\left( \\frac{113}{60} \\right) + d = 8\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{64}{60} - \\frac{16}{10} + \\frac{452}{60} + d = 8 \\implies \\frac{64 - 96 + 452}{60} + d = 8 \\implies \\frac{420}{60} + d = 8 \\implies 7 + d = 8 \\implies d = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the polynomial is:\n\\[\np(x) = \\frac{1}{60}x^3 - \\frac{1}{10}x^2 + \\frac{113}{60}x + 1\n\\]\n\nFinally, we find \\( p(12) \\):\n\\[\np(12) = \\frac{1}{60}(12^3) - \\frac{1}{10}(12^2) + \\frac{113}{60}(12) + 1 = \\frac{1}{60}(1728) - \\frac{1}{10}(144) + \\frac{113}{60}(12) + 1\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1728}{60} - \\frac{144}{10} + \\frac{1356}{60} + 1 = 28.8 - 14.4 + 22.6 + 1 = 38\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{38}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{38}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
